   "citationRecall": 0,
   "text": "The free tier is limited by requests per day, not by tokens. The free tier caps at 50 requests a day, while the models behind it offer 128k–512k of context. A turn costing three or four of them — the capability probe, the loop, the forced final call — is about fourteen questions before the panel starts reporting an outage that is not one. The two rotations are the same argument at two levels, and both are metered by the thing that catches people out: **requests per day**."
  },
