   "citationRecall": 0,
   "text": "To install DocPilot in a VitePress site, you need to configure the `docPilot` export in your VitePress config file. The CLI `npx docpilot index` walks markdown and writes static files, including `manifest.json`, chunk shards, vectors, and document frequencies. The config file is searched in six places, in order, with the VitePress paths coming first. The file must export `docPilot` by name, and the settings include `product`, `docsDir`, `chat`, and `embed`. For example:\n\n```js [docs/.vitepress/config.mjs]\nexport const docPilot = {\n  product: 'Acme Editor',\n  docsDir: 'docs',\n  chat: { provider: 'openai', model: 'gpt-4o-mini' },\n  embed: 'auto',\n}\n```\n\nAdditionally, you can use the `vitepress-plugin-llms` plugin to integrate DocPilot with VitePress. The full configuration is detailed in the VitePress section of the installation guide."
  },
