   "observed": "answer",
   "text": "To configure Algolia DocSearch crawling for your site, you need to set up the `ragBase` option in your Docusaurus configuration. This option specifies the base path where the index is served from. Here is an example configuration:\n\n```js\n['@cloflin/docpilot/docusaurus', {\n  config: ai.themeConfig,\n  highlighter: 'shiki',      // or 'none'\n  ragBase: '/rag',           // where the index is served from\n  styles: true,              // include the two stylesheets\n  selectors: { search: '.DocSearch-Button' },\n}]\n```\n\nThe `ragBase` value should be set to the path where your index is hosted. This ensures that the crawling process can locate and use the index correctly."
